    <!-- ── W/Mo with Mending wink (see WaMoEasterEgg) ─────────────────────
         Wamo* = the W/Mo speaks (team build) ; Player* = the app addresses the user (single build).
         The index is the number of heals BESIDES Mending, from 1 to 7. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Title">W/Mo</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo1">Hey, how about something more useful? I've already got Mending!</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo2">I've got Mending, remember? Nothing's killing me!</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo3">How about we take an attack skill instead?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo4">Four heals plus Mending. The party Monk can take the night off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo5">Five heals. I'm telling you, Mending had it covered.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo6">Six heals. I literally cannot die. Or kill anything, but still.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Wamo7">Seven heals and Mending. There. I'm a wall. A very supportive wall.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player1">You've already got Mending — what could possibly kill you?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player2">A second heal? Mending is already holding that bar together.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player3">Three heals. At this rate nobody is dying — least of all the enemy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player4">Four heals on a Warrior. Somewhere, a Monk is crying.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player5">Five heals plus Mending. Two slots left, in case you fancy hitting something.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player6">Six heals and Mending. This Warrior is now officially harmless.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Egg.Player7">Eight slots, eight heals. Congratulations — you have built the ultimate Warrior/Monk.</sys:String>

    <!-- ── GWRank (Extras ▸ Send to GWRank) ───────────────────────────── -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Menu.ExtrasGwRankSend">Send to GWRank...</sys:String>
